[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3554814940","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3554814940","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3554814940,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7T4ivc","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-19T22:06:42Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T22:06:42Z","body":"The change is correct, if `get_viewport()->get_popup_base_transform()` is identity then it returns `get_global_transform_with_canvas()` indeed:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15a13eed39d902fafb14ca0637c5827c80b2bc9/scene/main/canvas_item.cpp#L175-L179\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe faulty description was added in #59108 (cc @KoBeWi), the same issue is present for `Control.get_screen_position` method, should also be fixed:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15a13eed39d902fafb14ca0637c5827c80b2bc9/scene/gui/control.cpp#L1470-L1474\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15a13eed39d902fafb14ca0637c5827c80b2bc9/doc/classes/Control.xml#L492-L504\r\n\r\nNot sure how exactly the line `496` should be reworded (cc @Mickeon), possibly something like:\r\n```\r\nEquals to [code]get_global_transform_with_canvas().origin[/code] if the window is embedded (see [member Viewport.gui_embed_subwindows]).\r\n```\r\nor:\r\n```\r\nEquals to [code]get_screen_transform().origin[/code]. See: [method CanvasItem.get_screen_transform].\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso the code example in there is incorrect in general case (i.e. is not always correct):\r\n```gdscript\r\n# Incorrect:\r\npopup_menu.position = get_screen_position() + get_local_mouse_position()\r\n\r\n# Correct would be:\r\npopup_menu.position = get_screen_position() + get_screen_transform().basis_xform(get_local_mouse_position())\r\npopup_menu.position = get_screen_transform() * get_local_mouse_position()\r\npopup_menu.position = get_viewport()->get_mouse_position() # If I checked the source right.\r\n```\r\n\r\nInterestingly, it seems `get_screen_position() + some_local_position` is used [in many places across the codebase](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agodotengine%2Fgodot+get_screen_position%28%29+%2B&type=code). I'm guessing that's where you took it from @KoBeWi.\r\nThis will work fine as long as `get_screen_transform().basis_xform(some_local_position) == some_local_position`. Which within the editor is likely the case as there's no rotation or scaling involved for the editor controls.\r\n\r\nAs a proof here's a misplaced popup after rotating SceneTreeEditor:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a67b22fe-ac21-40b1-900e-fb4b19546e9e\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3554814940/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3557864142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3557864142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3557864142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UELLO","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T12:44:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T12:44:46Z","body":"> The faulty description was added in #59108 (cc @KoBeWi), the same issue is present for `Control.get_screen_position` method, should also be fixed:\r\n\r\nThanks for your comment, i will add the modifications you suggested in `Control.get_screen_position method` doc.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3557864142/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586510845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3586510845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3586510845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vxc_9","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T15:41:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T15:41:55Z","body":"Static check failed, is it caused by blank lines? I am a beginner and not sure how to solve it. Sorry for submitting so many times.😭","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586510845/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586825673","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3586825673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3586825673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vyp3J","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T17:11:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T17:11:45Z","body":"> is it caused by blank lines?\r\n\r\nThat's correct, and it's absolutely okay. The [static check is failing](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/19740528271/job/56563075098?pr=112952) because no trailing spaces are allowed, including tabs on otherwise empty lines. So the tabs should be removed both at line 500 and 503. You can say it's my fault for [suggesting the code as it was](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#discussion_r2568748083).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586825673/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3589038433","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3589038433","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3589038433,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V7GFh","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T11:53:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T11:53:53Z","body":"> Static check failed, is it caused by blank lines? I am a beginner and not sure how to solve it. Sorry for submitting so many times.😭\r\n\r\nYou can automatically force correct formatting using provided pre-commit hooks, see [Using clang-format locally](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html#using-clang-format-locally) docs.\r\n\r\nAlso be sure to make the PR have a single commit. `fixup` on subsequent commits while `rebase`-ing should do. See [The interactive rebase](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/organization/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#the-interactive-rebase) docs.\r\nContributors usually firstly apply whatever changes needed locally, and only then (after everything is as desired) force push to update the PR - this generates less noise for others.\r\n\r\nThe linked docs should be sufficient for you to resolve this, but in case you still have some problems with git/clang setup etc. then you could ask for help in https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/new-contributors.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3589038433/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3592718419","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3592718419","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3592718419,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WJIhT","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-30T15:44:49Z","updated_at":"2025-11-30T16:54:02Z","body":"> You can automatically force correct formatting using provided pre-commit hooks, see [Using clang-format locally](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html#using-clang-format-locally) docs.\r\n> \r\n> Also be sure to make the PR have a single commit. `fixup` on subsequent commits while `rebase`-ing should do. See [The interactive rebase](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/organization/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#the-interactive-rebase) docs. Contributors usually firstly apply whatever changes needed locally, and only then (after everything is as desired) force push to update the PR - this generates less noise for others.\r\n\r\nThank you for the link. I apologize for the late reply because I spent one day learning git and another day studying the hook and rebase. It seems I've only managed to get half of it right. Although the format is correctly fixed, it seems that I have created a bunch of new commits again.😞","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3592718419/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3592914973","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3592914973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3592914973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WJ4gd","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-30T17:33:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-30T17:46:46Z","body":"Ohhhhhhhhh my god, it seems like I did it! I just watched another video tutorial on _rebase_ and finally understood some of the principles. I've successfully cleaned up both the formatting and the commit history! So happy—time for sleep!😙","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3592914973/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3595892252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112952#issuecomment-3595892252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112952","id":3595892252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WVPYc","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"creat